Here's the full breakdown for your couple:

---

## EC Loan Capacity — $18,000/month Combined Income

| Constraint | Cap | Monthly Instalment |
|---|---|---|
| **TDSR 55%** | $9,900/month | (not binding) |
| **MSR 30%** | **$5,400/month** | **← binding for EC** |

MSR is the binding constraint — EC is treated like an HDB purchase, so the 30% MSR cap applies on top of TDSR.

---

## Maximum Loan Quantum

| Tenure | Rate | Max Loan | Max Price (75% LTV) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **25 years** | 1.5% | ~**$1.35M** | ~**$1.80M** |
| **30 years** | 1.5% | ~**$1.56M** | ~**$2.09M** |

---

## Cash at OTP (5% — cannot use CPF)

| Tenure | Price | Min Cash |
|---|---|---|
| 25-yr | $1.80M | ~$90,000 |
| 30-yr | $2.09M | ~$104,000 |

---

## Practical Recommendation

Target **$1.70M–$1.90M** purchase price if on a 25-year loan — this keeps the instalment within the MSR cap with buffer for rate rises above 1.5%. If comfortable with 30 years, up to ~$2.0M is serviceable, but banks stress-test at higher rates, so actual approval may be lower.

The 5% cash at OTP is the first liquidity gate — confirm the couple has that in cash (not CPF) before shortlisting ECs.


